# ⚠⚠ v2901 (#60) — THE VAULT LANE'S MEMORY IS MACHINE-LOCAL AND MUST NOT TRAVEL.
# `.vault_autoread.json` holds what THIS console's vault lane has read, how many attempts each
# reel cost it, and which reels it has RETIRED — stopped paying to sweep. Those decisions are about
# the reels on THIS disk.
#
# This repo is worked from two machines (the Mac ships, the Windows box pulls and tests). A tracked
# store would hand one machine's retirements to the other, whose hist/ holds different reels
# entirely — so the lane would skip reels it has never seen and re-buy ones it had ruled out, which
# is the exact defect #60 exists to end, re-entered through git.
#
# ⚠ REG-2461 (#181) - its sibling, the console's slowest-request record, is per-machine state too. It
# used to be the TRACKED tv/.status_worst.json, kept as "the 612,893 ms request that answered #28" -
# but the running console rewrote it on every new worst, so what shipped to every PC was one console's
# record (by v3406 his Mac's 1,773,092 ms request), and a fresh PC published it as its own worst.
# The console now writes only `.status_worst.here.json` below. The tracked file stays as it is
# (deleting it would make `git pull --ff-only` refuse on a PC where it is locally modified) and
# nothing writes it again.
tv/.vault_autoread.json

