# ══ v3187 — FIXTURE PACKS ARE NEVER COMMITTED ════════════════════════════════════════════════
# `tv/guest_fixture_pack.py` cuts these from HIS REAL REELS — actual frames of his game, 2.7 MB
# per pack. They are scrubbed of his machine's identifiers, which is not the same as being his to
# publish. THIS REPO IS PUBLIC. Packs travel to the box by rsync, never by git.
# ⚠⚠ v3199 — `fixtures/` IS NO LONGER IGNORED, BY HIS EXPLICIT CALL.
# 2026-09-16: "make it so they are uploaded with my reels" / "make it public no problem".
# I put both roads to him — a private SSH host for the Linux box, or the repo, which is public
# and permanent — and recommended the private one. He chose the repo, knowing that.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS THAT THEY SHIP: Grok Bot's box has no footage, so its SHELF renders blank and
# every visual pass it has ever done on that panel was about an empty room. The pack loader
# already defaults to `<repo>/fixtures`, so a box with nothing but a clone now stages them with
# no transport to configure. PROVEN, not assumed: loaded into a scratch mirror exactly as the box
# would -> 5 packs, 5 sessions, 5 reels, 77 files, every one flagged fixture:true.
#
# WHAT WAS CHECKED BEFORE HIS FRAMES BECAME PERMANENT: 0 leak hits across every text byte of all
# five packs (home paths, email, tokens, install ids, hostnames), all five verify, ~13 MB total,
# and 3 frames looked at by eye across 3 packs — title screen, real stash gameplay, logo — with
# no account name and no character name. The remaining 69 frames are UNKNOWN by eye; his capture
# never films the character panel (REG-340), which is the one screen that would carry a name.
# test_the_shipped_packs_are_staged_not_his_live_footage re-runs the leak audit on every run, so
# the next pack anyone adds is held to the bar the first five cleared.

# ⚠⚠ v3259 — HIS FOOTAGE AND HIS JOURNAL MUST NEVER BE COMMITTED. THIS REPO IS PUBLIC.
# tv/tvd-reel-seed-small.tgz is a guest-seat fixture pack built by the reel-seed tooling. At
# 97.84 MB it carried `sessions.jsonl` (his 3.4 MB journal) and `frames/hist/reel_*` (his actual
# gameplay footage) onto the public remote, and it went in through a `git add -A`. GitHub warned
# at 97.84 MB against a HARD limit of 100 MB, so it was also ~2 MB from refusing every push.
# The seed pack is a real artefact and is kept ON DISK; it is simply never tracked.
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
tv/tvd-reel-seed*

# ⚠ his own saved product links — swept in by a `git add -A` in v3456 and published to a
# PUBLIC repo by accident. Ignored so it cannot happen again.
deeplink.txt
